echo '<div class="page-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">WRLC Claims Returned</p><h1>About this site</h1></div><a href="login.php">Sign in</a></div>';
echo '<section class="card"><p>The Claims Returned site helps consortium library staff coordinate searches for items patrons report as returned but that are not yet showing as checked in. Staff can look up Alma patron accounts and checked-out items, open and track cases, record search results, and communicate case outcomes.</p><p>Alma remains the source of truth for patron and circulation records. Search notes are saved to the patron record in Alma. When patron email updates are enabled, email is sent when a case opens, closes, or reopens.</p></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>Using the site</h2><ol><li><strong>Sign in</strong> with your consortium staff account.</li><li><strong>Open a case.</strong> Choose New case, enter the patron ID, and look up their account.</li><li><strong>Choose the item.</strong> Select the matching checked-out item from the patron’s loan list. Its details fill the case form.</li><li><strong>Set up the case.</strong> Confirm the patron and item details. Choose the case type, patron email preference, assigned staff member, and partner library details. The partner email is filled from the Resource Sharing Contact List when a match is available. You may enter multiple partner addresses separated by commas.</li><li><strong>Complete each search.</strong> On the case page, enter the search result, notes, and due date, then save. Search notes are added to Alma. The patron is not emailed after each search.</li><li><strong>Close a found case.</strong> Mark the item as found. Before saving, the site checks whether Alma shows it as checked in. If Alma still shows it checked out or cannot confirm its status, review the warning and make sure it has been checked in before you continue.</li><li><strong>Finish or reopen the case.</strong> A not-found case closes after the fourth search. If email updates are enabled, the patron receives the final outcome. Reopen a closed case if more searching is needed; the patron is notified when it is reopened.</li><li><strong>Review cases.</strong> The queue lists active cases; use Closed cases to view completed cases. A case’s Patron account accordion shows patron details and notes. Checked-out items appear during patron lookup when opening a new case.</li><li><strong>Open partner contacts.</strong> Use the Resource Sharing Contact List button in the header to view CLS, P2P, and ILL contacts.</li></ol></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>User</h2><p>A User can create, view, and update cases for their assigned institution and can view the Resource Sharing Contact List from the header.</p><ol><li>Look up the patron and select the item from their checked-out list.</li><li>Open the case, choose its type, and optionally assign an active staff account.</li><li>Record search outcomes and notes as each search is completed.</li><li>Update assignments, search dates, and patron contact preferences from the case page.</li><li>View the patron’s Alma details and notes and add a custom internal Alma note when needed.</li></ol><p>Users can view contacts but cannot add, edit, or delete them.</p></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>Super User</h2><p>A Super User can manage cases across institutions. In the queue, use the institution filter to view one institution or all institutions. Super Users can also manage accounts and resource-sharing contacts for their own institution.</p><ol><li>Create and manage cases for any active institution.</li><li>For your own institution, edit or disable accounts, change passwords, and delete User or Super User accounts. You cannot edit or delete Admin accounts.</li><li>View the Resource Sharing Contact List for all institutions; add, edit, or delete contacts only for your own institution.</li><li>Assign active staff accounts and update case workflow details.</li><li>View open and closed cases across the consortium and reopen cases when necessary.</li><li>Delete individual Alma patron notes when required.</li><li>Open <strong>Institution accounts</strong> from the site navigation to create a User account for your own institution. You can enter the account manually or look up the person in Alma.</li></ol><p>Super Users can create User accounts only for their own institution. Admins can manage accounts and contacts across all institutions, including Admin accounts and role assignments.</p></section>';

echo '<section class="card"><h2>Admin</h2><p>An Admin has all Super User case-management access and can also manage user accounts and Resource Sharing Contact List entries across all institutions.</p><ol><li>Open Admin from the site navigation.</li><li>Find accounts by name, email, or institution, or look up a staff member by Alma user ID.</li><li>Create accounts, assign an institution and role, edit account details, disable or delete accounts, or set a replacement password.</li><li>Add, edit, delete, or import contact rows in the Resource Sharing Contact List.</li><li>Use the case page to delete a case or delete an individual Alma patron note when needed.</li></ol></section>';

